infinity is a puzzling concept not the  notion of potential infinity that  numbers go on forever but the concept of  infinity as an actual complete  manipulable object  does infinity really exist or is it just  part of the fabric of our imaginations  assuming actual infinity leads to  unsettling consequences numbers like 1 2  3 4 are countably infinite but between  each of them say between 1 &amp; 2 there is  an uncountably infinite continuum of  real numbers such as 1 point 1 1 point 1  1 1 point 1 1 1 1 and so on the two sets  real numbers and counting numbers are  both infinite but have different sizes  some infinities are bigger than others  so does actual infinity exist or just  the idea of potential infinity most  people simply ignore the paradoxes which  lie in abstract realms with few  practical or scientific ramifications  but for some mathematicians their  presence raises concerns and might  unravel the foundations of the entire  field of mathematics
 

